From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:18:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 179/192] wifi: ath11k: do not deinit the core of a device that
 never registered

Removing a device whose firmware never came up (no QMI server, so the
core was never started) runs ath11k_core_deinit(), which stops the CE
pipes and reaps rings that were never set up in the HAL: a NULL
dereference in ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin() from
ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes(). Shutdown already skips the deinit for such a
device; take the QMI-failure path in remove() too, and unregister the
PM notifier on that path for AHB as PCI does.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c | 5 ++++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
index 1784916..316c0d2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -1383,10 +1383,13 @@ static void ath11k_ahb_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct ath11k_base *ab = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags)) {
+	/* Without firmware the rings were never set up: core_deinit would reap them. */
+	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags) ||
+	    !test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags)) {
 		ath11k_ahb_power_down(ab, false);
 		ath11k_debugfs_soc_destroy(ab);
 		ath11k_qmi_deinit_service(ab);
+		ath11k_core_pm_notifier_unregister(ab);
 		goto qmi_fail;
 	}
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
index 6d82779..94f1380 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
@@ -1206,7 +1206,9 @@ static void ath11k_pci_remove(struct pci_dev *pdev)
 
 	ath11k_pci_set_irq_affinity_hint(ab_pci, NULL);
 
-	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags)) {
+	/* Without firmware the rings were never set up: core_deinit would reap them. */
+	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_QMI_FAIL, &ab->dev_flags) ||
+	    !test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_REGISTERED, &ab->dev_flags)) {
 		ath11k_pci_power_down(ab, false);
 		ath11k_debugfs_soc_destroy(ab);
 		ath11k_qmi_deinit_service(ab);
